title: A Debate on the Constitution
subtitle: The right and PSL “Piast” want to repair the March Constitution; PPS states which motions it supports.
new-page: true
tags: pl_event
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishProjects.constitutionDebateDue(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Event politics.constitution_debate (Z — 0.56, item 2 of 5 X 2026; Z — 0.82, the user's decisions of 21 X 2026): it opens
// the constitutional debate once, in December 1924. On this page PPS marks the motions it supports, in its order; the
// Constitutional Committee then brings them to the floor by a monthly chance and the urgent card polish_constitution_vote
// puts each to both chambers (technical reference 7.6). 0 T. The facts of the text are in HISTORICAL_SOURCES.md.
PolishProjects.openConstitutionDebate(Q);
PolishProjects.debateView(Q);
!}

= A debate on the constitution

At its congress on 26 October 1924 the Popular National Union (ZLN) adopted a resolution on the “repair of the constitution”: a President who may dissolve the Sejm, a Senate equal to the Sejm, fewer deputies, a narrower immunity and a constitutional tribunal. In December 1924 the congress of PSL “Piast” also declared a change of the constitution necessary. The Sejm opens a constitutional debate.

A debate does not mean a vote: the Constitutional Committee may work for months. Mark the motions PPS will support, in the order of their importance. Each month the Committee may bring one of them to the floor: the first on our list has a chance of about 17%, the second 10%, the third 7%, each later one 3.5%. The Sejm and the Senate then vote on the same day, and a change needs two thirds of the votes for and against in both chambers. A motion PPS does not support does not come to a vote.

Our list: [+ pl_con_draft_text +].

- @m_democratic_guarantees
- @m_church_separation
- @m_constructive_vonc
- @m_referendum
- @m_presidential_arbitration
- @m_labour_chamber
- @m_unicameral
- @declare

